#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7a75441-d233-5a64-8d87-b3138c2d31be" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88203b12-b694-5d1b-aef7-4b0bfa03a317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2 π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{25}ρ 3 cos ⁡ θ sin ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126638} {:answer/id #uuid "99157e6a-5a60-542f-8885-7c827373d41f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{25}ρ 2 cos ⁡ θ sin 3 ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126639} {:answer/id #uuid "f98f61e8-d019-5899-9494-5b179c282c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2 π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{5}ρ 2 sin ⁡ θ sin 3 ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126640} {:answer/id #uuid "2be27154-72e7-5290-83a6-86c4a4a8c045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2 π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{5}ρ 2 cos ⁡ θ sin ⁡ θ sin 3 ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126641} {:answer/id #uuid "570ad61f-5a8a-523a-b583-0195f04ac45a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{5}ρ 3 cos ⁡ θ sin ⁡ θ sin 2 ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126642}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e2fca817-6a22-5c0a-8bd9-eb65ba7787e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49e9a4ed-cc02-552b-850f-590a1eabb508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{25}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374008} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6da4e6-4d70-5d57-830d-2c3550356100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{25}{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374009} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c418fd-e2e2-58e2-b16d-b624dda6a4c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374010} {:answer/id #uuid "0d81db19-07f6-520d-bd7f-8449d3b4156e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374011} {:answer/id #uuid "91e95a72-f432-5a4d-9e2e-324cee6736c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91e95a72-f432-5a4d-9e2e-324cee6736c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374012} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d2f399-c08f-57b6-b31d-d84d8b9705c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "699f2901-2747-5828-8f8f-087336e97be3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161754" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=25.$\nExpress the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\n$$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $5$ centered at the origin. \nAs a result, in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 5,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\cdot \\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{{\\rho }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{3}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7a75441-d233-5a64-8d87-b3138c2d31be" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Triple Integral Defined Over a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9282e885-d570-5d72-9968-8527160b169f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{9}ρ 3 sin ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128018} {:answer/id #uuid "048690e5-c379-58d8-ac2f-79765dfd32aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{3}ρ 4 cos ⁡ ϕ sin ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128019} {:answer/id #uuid "528058ee-b8cf-5ca5-b635-c49112468757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{3}ρ 3 sin ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128020} {:answer/id #uuid "57d1d358-75e3-59df-80ce-35c3d6d36295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2 π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{3}ρ 4 cos ⁡ ϕ sin ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128021} {:answer/id #uuid "66a974b1-4913-5a37-a4cb-eda26703eb43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2 π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2π}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{3}ρ 4 cos ⁡ ϕdρdθdϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128022}] :answer-field/id #uuid "167cbf2b-6403-547f-9f10-b1af15a48555" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aa22172-aed4-5605-92ab-59f3b9c082a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375137} {:answer/id #uuid "47674ef2-eb40-5ead-b7da-b61decf7c865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{9}{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375138} {:answer/id #uuid "a76f3460-fc95-508d-924f-bca258671c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375139} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0a05b0-be97-5bf2-ae2d-2d653d7ac4e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\rho }^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375140} {:answer/id #uuid "6976b7cc-768c-59b4-88b8-9e266d9b514a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6976b7cc-768c-59b4-88b8-9e266d9b514a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375141} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d1c327d-1302-5a46-953f-a8e3268dd875" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e21b1a1-dd1a-5b1e-a6f4-aca8044792b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-40073" :question/problem "The region $R$ is enclosed inside the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9.$\nExpress the following triple integral in spherical polar coordinates. \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}z\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\,{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\n$$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $3$ centered at the origin. \nAs a result, in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=z\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\cdot \\rho  \\\\  & ={\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}z\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
